WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.549 --> 00:00:16.590
You don’t have to be an intellectual to
recognize how much season 8 sucked,

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.660
especially in comparison to the previous seasons.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:23.680
Even casual fans recognized it, which the
official ratings clearly show.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:27.789
My channel grew infamous for criticizing the
show in season 8

00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:32.529
episode after episode for bad writing and
bad continuity and the general lack of logic.

00:00:32.529 --> 00:00:35.760
It's not a secret that the show had a potential
to become the best show ever

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.370
(which it still is to me even with the horrible
final season

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:44.000
just because it had the absolute perfect 6
seasons.. yes season 7 was bad as well in

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.000
my opinion).

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.829
But Season 8 was a disaster.

00:00:46.829 --> 00:00:49.520
Even actors, who earn money by excellent acting
skills,

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.510
can’t hide how disappointed they are with
season 8.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:55.590
The story was rushed, character arcs destroyed.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:57.519
There should have been 10 seasons.

00:00:57.519 --> 00:01:01.500
Entire season 8 and the first part of season
9 should have been the long night,

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.140
war against the Night King, the second part
of season 9, and entire season 10 about Dany's

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.539
descent into madness and war against Cersei.

00:01:08.539 --> 00:01:11.000
That's what HBO wanted as well.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.750
They tried to convince them to do 10 seasons
but were lucky enough to even get this much

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.429
from D and D because they originally wanted
only 7 seasons.

00:01:17.429 --> 00:01:22.880
In truth, HBO did not even get a full season,
they only got 3 extra episodes out of David

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:23.880
and Dan.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.729
Their planned final season 7 was supposed
to have 10 episodes,

00:01:26.729 --> 00:01:31.270
but when HBO convinced them to make 8 seasons,
they reduced the number of episodes from 10

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:35.069
to 7 for season 7 and had only 6 for season
8.

00:01:35.069 --> 00:01:39.509
Anyways, in this video, we are going to talk
about every single error in season 8 episode

00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:40.509
1.

00:01:40.509 --> 00:01:44.099
Before we dive into the series, I just want
to highlight that all the criticism is directed

00:01:44.099 --> 00:01:48.220
towards the showrunners and not towards actors
and the whole crew that did their best with

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:50.500
the horrible scripts they’ve got.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:54.720
Actors and everyone involved in Game of Thrones
except for D&amp;D deserve a standing OVATION

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.440
for their hard work over the years.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:58.520
With that said, let’s get into it!

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:02.810
The season 8 premiere starts with a nice callback
and parallels to the season 1 premiere

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:22.900
which is quickly ruined with Tyrion's awful
joke.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:27.650
When you don't have the capability to continue
Tyrion's brilliant arc from the earlier seasons,

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:31.810
dropping his IQ considerably ever since you've
passed the book material, this is what you

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:32.810
get.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:36.570
Arya’s look at dragons gave me hope that
this season might have some story continuity

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:39.090
because she seemed so happy to see them.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:43.920
Arya has always admired dragons and especially
the Targaryen Queen who rode them.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:48.530
We learned that early on in season 2 episode
7 when Arya reveals to Tywin Lannister how

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:53.500
she adores Aegon the Conqueror's sisters,
Rhaenys and Visenya, with the latter being

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:54.500
her heroine.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:03:00.380
I guess Arya kind of forgot her character
was supposed to like Dany.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:07.260
Sansa’s look at dragons when they fly over
Winterfell gives me such a Littlefinger vibe,

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:11.400
she sees something so powerful and doesn’t
see a way not to bend her knee to such power

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.710
and it bothers her which we clearly see when
she greets Dany.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:17.730
Still, Sansa said she's a slow learner, but
she learns,

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:22.290
then how come didn't she learn from Littlefinger
to give fake smiles and pretend she likes

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.240
Dany,
a reaction which should have been natural

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:27.290
in the first place
because the Dragon Queen has come to save

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:28.610
your home and your people.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:33.150
When Jon and Bran reunited and Bran replied
to Jon's “You’re a man” with “Almost”,

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:37.040
I thought that reunion could have been done
better, but at that point, I was really looking

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.490
forward to how Bran’s story will play out,
I was excited that his story will finally

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:45.240
be somewhat exciting,
as, besides the tower of joy, his visions

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:48.380
and Hodor moment, Bran’s whole story was
rather boring.

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:52.910
In fact, it was so boring that the showrunners
did not even include Bran in the entirety

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:53.910
of season five.

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:57.620
Yes, that’s right, if you didn’t notice,
and I don’t blame you because the boy was

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:01.030
so boring,
Bran missed out the entire 5th season.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:05.250
I thought season 8 had all the potential to
redeem him from being this boring weird guy

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:09.430
to an interesting three-eyed raven filled
with visions and all the warging we could

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:10.430
witness.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:14.489
At the end, all Bran did was nothing, we saw
not one vision in season 8

00:04:14.489 --> 00:04:17.519
and the only thing Bran warged was a few ravens.

00:04:17.519 --> 00:04:21.269
And apparently, that’s the best story...

00:04:21.269 --> 00:04:26.979
I remember before season 8 aired how we all
thought Bran’s powers would be crucial against

00:04:26.979 --> 00:04:31.789
the Night King, after all, he did hype us
up by saying he needs to see better before

00:04:31.789 --> 00:04:33.029
the Night King arrives.

00:04:33.029 --> 00:04:36.849
Also, don't forget that tower of Joy vision
from the past in which he calls out to his

00:04:36.849 --> 00:04:38.569
father Ned who hears him.

00:04:38.569 --> 00:04:43.210
Well, all of that turned out to be of no significance
at all, it turned out to be nothing.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:45.749
They really did subvert our expectations...

00:04:45.749 --> 00:04:49.900
Northerners being unhappy with Dany’s arrival
at Winterfell makes no sense,

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:53.979
especially knowing they found out from Bran
that the Night King has a dragon in his army

00:04:53.979 --> 00:04:56.620
now
and has broken the wall and already started

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.570
his Conquest over the North.

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:01.949
Instead of their smug faces, and worrying
about what dragons eat

00:05:01.949 --> 00:05:06.039
and worrying about who has what title, they
should have cheered at the arrival of Dany,

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:08.409
her 2 dragons and her huge armies.

00:05:08.409 --> 00:05:13.339
I’m glad Jon Snow shuts Sansa and all the
petty northern lords by saying that without

00:05:13.339 --> 00:05:18.340
Dany and her army and her dragons, they wouldn’t
stand a chance … although I don't like his

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:20.189
statement “I had a choice.

00:05:20.189 --> 00:05:21.949
Keep my crown or protect the north.

00:05:21.949 --> 00:05:24.439
I chose the north” because that’s a lie.

00:05:24.439 --> 00:05:28.180
After Viserion was shot down and when they
were on the boat going to Kings Landing with

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:32.359
a kidnapped wight, Dany gave him her word
that she will march her armies north

00:05:32.359 --> 00:05:35.249
, and together they will destroy the Night
King.

00:05:35.249 --> 00:05:38.620
Jon then said “thank you Dany” on which
she replied with that she doesn't remember

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:43.620
who called her that last time, perhaps her
unpleasant brother Viserys on which Jon replied

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.469
“Alright, not Dany.

00:05:45.469 --> 00:05:49.990
How about my Queen?” and bent the knee,
not literally cause he was injured, but it

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:51.220
was pretty much it.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:54.949
So when Jon says ''I had a choice, keep my
crown or protect the north'',

00:05:54.949 --> 00:05:58.930
implying that Dany wouldn’t come if he did
not bend the knee -- is not true.

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:03.819
Guess D&amp;D kinda forgot about the entire boat
scene and about Jon Snow not being able to

00:06:03.819 --> 00:06:04.819
lie.

00:06:04.819 --> 00:06:08.610
Season 8 is rushed and full of errors.

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:13.830
Anyways, Tyrion then also tries to explain
to these petty northern lords

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:18.599
that without Jon Snow and his successful travel
south to convince the dragon Queen to help

00:06:18.599 --> 00:06:20.800
the North, they would all die.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:24.839
This is followed by possibly the most stupid
question in the show, which is Sansa’s question

00:06:24.839 --> 00:06:29.069
“May I ask, how are we meant to feed the
greatest army the world has ever seen?

00:06:29.069 --> 00:06:33.949
While I ensured our stores would last through
winter, I didn’t account for Dothraki, Unsullied,

00:06:33.949 --> 00:06:34.949
and two full-grown dragons.

00:06:34.949 --> 00:06:37.330
What do dragons eat, anyway?”.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.330
Really Sansa?

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:39.330
That’s your concern?

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.690
Will there be enough food until the Night
King attacks you tomorrow evening and what

00:06:42.690 --> 00:07:10.559
do dragons eat?

00:07:10.559 --> 00:07:14.069
Someone should sit her like a small child
and explain to her that not only does Winterfell

00:07:14.069 --> 00:07:18.270
stand no chance against the Night King without
Dany, but they would not even have the weapons

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:22.300
that are able to kill the Night King’s army
that Dany provided from Dragonstone.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:25.569
Dany literally has nothing to gain from this
allegiance with the North.

00:07:25.569 --> 00:07:28.960
She’s seen the Night King, she knows she
will lose far more of her own men

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:33.259
than the North could ever provide her and
still she decides to save the North.

00:07:33.259 --> 00:07:37.090
Dany should have pulled the Sansa move Sansa
did on Arya in season 7

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:40.389
about how without her the North didn't stand
a chance in a fight

00:07:40.389 --> 00:07:42.099
and she should be on her knees thanking her.

00:07:42.099 --> 00:07:46.460
At least Sansa does recognize in episode 2
that instead of being rude

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:48.680
she should have thanked her as soon as she
arrived.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:08:21.889
but then in episode 3 and all 

00:08:21.889 --> 00:08:27.830
the remaining episodes she’s back to her
power-hungry and ungrateful attitude.

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:43.490
Total shitshow!

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:47.480
Tyrion says “if anyone survives the war
to come, we’ll have Jon Snow to thank.

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:50.300
He risked his life to show us the threat is
real.

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:53.550
Thanks to his courage we have brought the
greatest army the world has ever seen.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:56.130
We have brought two large full grown dragons”.

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:59.310
Oh boy did you thank him after you all survived.

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:03.240
Not only did he save all of Westeros becuase
he convinced Dany to ally with the North and

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:07.889
defeat the Night King, but at the end he also
killed Dany to once again save Westeros from

00:09:07.889 --> 00:09:10.730
Dany
(Mad Queen the shity writers made her mad

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:14.550
in the span of one episode)
who intended to liberate all of Westeros by

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:16.130
burning down everything and everyone.

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:20.709
They, especially Tyrion, thanked him real
good at the end, not even mentioning his name

00:09:20.709 --> 00:09:24.990
at the great council when electing the King,
banishing him to the Wall.

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:29.199
To make things ever worse, the council was
literally made up of 90% of people who are

00:09:29.199 --> 00:09:34.460
good with Jon, most being his friends and
family, most of whom knew Jon was the rightful

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:35.460
king.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:38.420
When the question of the potential King came
in, nobody mentioned his name.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:40.959
I'll go hard on that when we come to that
episode.

00:09:40.959 --> 00:09:43.670
Anyways, back to the season 8 premiere.

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:48.120
Next we have a scene in which we see tons
and tons of dragonglass that they mined

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:51.920
and brought from Dragonstone to Winterfell
which is the only thing capable of killing

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:55.959
the Night King’s army, beside a few Valyrian
steel swords and fire.

00:09:55.959 --> 00:09:58.209
What was the purpose of showing all of this
dragonglass

00:09:58.209 --> 00:10:03.009
when in episode 3 we see that the entire Dothraki
cavalry who are on the first line of defence

00:10:03.009 --> 00:10:06.769
or should I say offence don’t even have
Dragonglass weapons

00:10:06.769 --> 00:10:11.459
and therefore 100 000 of them wouldn’t be
able to kill even one wight.

00:10:11.459 --> 00:10:16.870
Lucky for them Melisandre showed up unexpected,
out of nowhere and set their ARAKHS on fire.

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:29.500
Best writing ever!

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:32.839
Is she really saying that the Queen who instead
of going for the Iron Throne and remaining

00:10:32.839 --> 00:10:37.519
south
came to help her and the north is not a good

00:10:37.519 --> 00:10:38.519
queen?

00:10:38.519 --> 00:10:39.519
What?

00:10:39.519 --> 00:10:43.330
Sansa and Tyrion conversation had some good
parts with the two discussing the last time

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:47.670
they saw each other, especially when Sansa
says Joffrey’s wedding had its moments and

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:48.670
both smiled.

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:49.670
When Tyrion says to her “Many underestimated
you.

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:50.670
Most are dead now”
is a nice little throwback to this Tyrion’s

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:51.670
statement way back in early seasons.

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:52.670
Really hurts to see how the showrunners made
Tyrion go from one of the smartest people

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:57.340
in the realm to a complete fool who believes
Cersei will send army north and Sansa here

00:10:57.340 --> 00:11:00.480
mocks him for that.

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:06.069
They really thought we would be okay with
Sansa (who spent only a few years around Cersei)

00:11:06.069 --> 00:11:09.920
understanding her character and motives better
than Tyrion (Cersei’s brother who spent

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:12.930
most of his life with her).. yeah, right..

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:17.240
Tyrion and his plans being so idiotic in recent
times is not a testament how Tyrion’s character

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:21.069
is stupid because it’s not,
Tyrion is one of the smartest people in this

00:11:21.069 --> 00:11:23.709
world,
but its rather that showrunners were not smart

00:11:23.709 --> 00:11:26.040
enough
to do his character after the book material

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:27.040
ran out.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:28.040
Bran looking at him like, she’s right, I
saw it, you stupid.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:30.480
How drastically they reduced Tyrion’s IQ
is still beyond me.

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:35.350
Every single of Tyrion’s plans in seasons
7 and 8 were so bad and devastating for Dany

00:11:35.350 --> 00:11:39.600
that at one point (before being sent the leaks)
I was convinced Tyrion was a traitor working

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:40.930
for Cersei.

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:43.029
I even made a few videos about it.

00:11:43.029 --> 00:11:46.009
Jon-Arya reunion was actually alright for
some part.

00:11:46.009 --> 00:11:50.070
In my opinion, it could have been done better,
but compared to everything else, it was alright.

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:53.630
The hug and the first part of the conversation
was done just fine,

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:57.680
but then Arya goes on to stay on Sansa’s
side instead of supporting Jon

00:11:57.680 --> 00:12:01.070
who is obviously right about them needing
Dany.

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.759
Also that Arya’s now already infamous line
“Sansa is the smartest person I’ve ever

00:12:04.759 --> 00:12:10.160
met”
is such a punch to the face to all of us.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:12.650
Don't get me wrong, I’m okay with Sansa
being smart,

00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:16.260
she’s had years and years of learning to
play the Game of Thrones,

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:19.850
learning from some of the best, including
Cersei and Littlefinger,

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:22.580
but would the one who knows the game really
act like that towards Dany?

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:26.959
Can you see someone really politically smart
act like that towards their allies who came

00:12:26.959 --> 00:12:28.250
to save them?

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:32.759
Anyways, Arya saying Sansa is the smartest
person she’s ever met is plain stupid

00:12:32.759 --> 00:12:35.990
especially when you remember she met and spent
a good amount of time

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:38.649
with none other than mighty Tywin Lannister.

00:12:38.649 --> 00:12:42.910
Then again, Arya is not very good with words
which we learn later when she says for Dany

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:47.629
“I know a killer when I see one” right
after Dany burned down entire Kings Landing,

00:12:47.629 --> 00:12:49.129
killing one million people.

00:12:49.129 --> 00:12:50.260
Good call, Arya!

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:55.450
So yeah, Arya saying for Sansa to be the smartest
person she’s ever met makes no sense,

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:59.350
not only because Arya definitely met people
smarter than Sansa,

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:04.370
but also because there was nothing Sansa displayed
in season 7 or 8 that would lead Arya to say

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:05.370
that.

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:07.600
Sansa almost fell for Littlefinger’s game
in season 7.

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:12.699
That’s right, it wasn’t Sansa manipulating
him, it was once again her being manipulated

00:13:12.699 --> 00:13:17.220
during the entire season until Bran told her
behind the scenes what’s Littlefinger really

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:18.940
about and what he did.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:23.310
This was confirmed by an actor who plays Bran
Stark as well as by the showrunners.

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:24.590
So there’s that.

00:13:24.590 --> 00:13:27.910
Also if Jon’s “how did you sneak up on
me” was meant to foreshadow Arya sneaking

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:32.439
up on the Night King two episodes later in
this same place, that’s not smart foreshadowing,

00:13:32.439 --> 00:13:36.079
because here Jon is alone,
so it’s explainable and logical that a year

00:13:36.079 --> 00:13:40.810
or two of training to become a stealthy assassin
would result in her being able to sneak up

00:13:40.810 --> 00:13:44.050
on a person who is alone,
but her sneaking up on the Night King who

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:48.910
is surrounded by all the White Walkers
and his entire army of the dead, yeah that’s

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:49.910
bs!

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:53.149
And btw as you can see, there is literally
nothing Arya could have used to come close

00:13:53.149 --> 00:13:59.589
to the Night King without being spotted nor
something to use to jump on him the way she

00:13:59.589 --> 00:14:00.589
did.

00:14:00.589 --> 00:14:03.509
Their reunion ends with Arya saying to Jon
something along the line

00:14:03.509 --> 00:14:07.889
“don’t forget you are my and Sansa’s
family with Jon’s face being like “what?”.

00:14:07.889 --> 00:14:12.339
At a time I thought Bran probably told Arya
and Sansa about Jon’s parentage

00:14:12.339 --> 00:14:16.660
and that’s why Arya says this but no, we
see them learn that later from Bran

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:19.690
(instead of learning it from Jon which made
me so angry).

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:23.089
So her saying this to Jon Snow here makes
no sense.

00:14:23.089 --> 00:14:25.459
Down south, things are not going great either.

00:14:25.459 --> 00:14:29.519
Euron tells Yara his ship Silence is full
of mutes, thank god they are still holding

00:14:29.519 --> 00:14:34.050
continuity in some parts of the story, oh
nevermind, they later kind of forgot they

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:36.320
had no tongues when they yelled and shouted.

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:40.680
Euron’s complete character is just a joke,
I honestly feel bad for the actor who was

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:45.339
so pumped to play Euron because he’s a big
